`glVertexAttribDivisor` and `glDrawArraysInstanced` were called without the `ext.` prefix while all other OpenGL extension functions in the file used `context.extensions`. This inconsistency can cause compilation/linking errors on platforms where these functions aren't directly available.

### Changes

- Added `ext.` prefix to all `glVertexAttribDivisor` calls (4 occurrences)
- Added `ext.` prefix to `glDrawArraysInstanced` call

```cpp
// Before
glVertexAttribDivisor(static_cast<GLuint>(instancePosAttrib_), 1);
glDrawArraysInstanced(GL_TRIANGLE_FAN, 0, 4, static_cast<GLsizei>(instanceData_.size()));

// After
ext.glVertexAttribDivisor(static_cast<GLuint>(instancePosAttrib_), 1);
ext.glDrawArraysInstanced(GL_TRIANGLE_FAN, 0, 4, static_cast<GLsizei>(instanceData_.size()));
```

